Subject: [PATCH 15/32] doc: define the --flash-info-json contract

Consumers (ie label generation that refuses to print a label when a
flash fact was not collected) need the meaning of each field, not a
printed report:

- unique_id.state: read / blank, and none with a note (read from the
  chip: no factory ID) versus none with a null note (openFPGALoader
  knows no unique ID command for this part, which says nothing about
  the silicon); a failed read is an error and no file is written.
- part and database sizes are looked up from the JEDEC ID, not read,
  and one ID may be shared by several parts (ie 0xc22017).
- format is fixed and version is increased on any field change.
- the version string does not tell whether --flash-info exists: check
  --help.
- on Xilinx, every read, including the JEDEC ID, goes through the
  spiOverJtag bridge and replaces the running design.

